<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Korea and Japan</p><h1 class="st-title">Heungyo</h1><p class="st-meta">1029 CE – 1030 CE · capital Dongjing (Liaoyang)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A brief attempt to revive Balhae, proclaimed at Liaoyang in 1029 by a descendant of its founder in revolt against the Khitan Liao dynasty.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1029 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dae-yeon-rim">Dae Yeon-rim</a>, a descendant of Balhae's founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dae-joyeong">Dae Joyeong</a> serving as an officer of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/liao-dynasty">Liao dynasty</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaoyang">Dongjing</a>, modern Liaoyang, rebelled against Khitan rule, killed local officials and proclaimed a new state called Heungyo, Xingliao in Chinese, with its own era name.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The rebellion drew on <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/balhae">Balhae</a> descendants in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a> region who resented Khitan taxes and labour demands. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dae-yeon-rim">Dae Yeon-rim</a> sent envoys to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/goryeo">Goryeo</a> asking for help, but Goryeo declined to intervene.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a> armies besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaoyang">Dongjing</a>, and in 1030 an officer opened the city gates; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dae-yeon-rim">Dae Yeon-rim</a> was captured and the state ended after about a year. Some of his followers fled to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/goryeo">Goryeo</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1029 CE – 1030 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Korea and Japan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:80.18%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1029 CE – 1030 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dongjing (Liaoyang)</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Dae Yeon-rim</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Xingliao, Hungyo</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1030&amp;focus=heungyo" aria-label="Heungyo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7581 918 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Heungyo lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7901 1174L7866 1006"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7866 1006h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7901 1174h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7901 1174h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dongjing. <a href="/atlas?year=1030&amp;focus=heungyo">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
